<title>INDIA: India Jan six-sector industrial output up 2.9 pct.</title>
<headline>India Jan six-sector industrial output up 2.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's six-sector industrial production index, representing the main infrastructure sectors, rose 2.9 percent in January over the same month in 1996, a government statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>In the period April 1996-December 1997, the index increased 3.3 percent compared with the year-earlier period, it said.  </p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    SIX-SECTOR INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION     Jan 97   Apr 96-Jan 97</p>
<p>    Electricity				   +5.0	  +3.8</p>
<p>    Coal					    +2.5	  +5.7</p>
<p>    Saleable steel				+0.5	  +2.8</p>
<p>    Crude petroleum			     -9.2	  -8.8</p>
<p>    Petroleum Refinery Products	     +9.7	  +6.9</p>
<p>    Cement					  +7.2	  +9.8</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    SIX INFRASTRUCTURE INDUSTRIES	   +2.9	  +3.3</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Note: The index includes six sectors accounting for 28.8 percent of the overall index of industrial production. The figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
